# Programmatic API

The `cargo-upwell` library exposes the same target discovery and isolated probe boundary as the CLI without requiring terminal parsing. This section owns Rust integration; CLI rendering and shell exit behavior remain under <GuideRef slug="cargo-upwell/cli">CLI</GuideRef>.

## Choose an API level

| Task | Guide |
|---|---|
| construct discovery input, run a probe, retain `ProbeEnvelope`, or query the canonical graph | <GuideRef slug="cargo-upwell/programmatic-api/discovery-and-probes">Discovery and probes</GuideRef> |
| run presentation-neutral `check` or `doctor` policy and consume one `CommandReport` | <GuideRef slug="cargo-upwell/programmatic-api/command-reports">Command reports</GuideRef> |

## Shared prerequisites

Mirror Cargo target and feature selection exactly, move synchronous calls to a blocking worker in async applications, and validate semantic schema requirements before consuming persisted or remote evidence.
